cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Precedent: a self-evolving Claude Code harness with a verified self-modification loop"
message: "If you use this software or the method, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Linxiushen
    website: "https://github.com/Linxiushen"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Linxiushen/precedent"
url: "https://github.com/Linxiushen/precedent"
abstract: >-
  Coding agents routinely rewrite their own memory, skills and configuration.
  The step nobody implements is acceptance: deciding whether a self-modification
  should be kept. Precedent turns a user's correction into a test with planted
  ground truth — the temporal birth gate — and ships the acceptance stack around
  it: a paired anytime-valid e-process, a per-task regression floor, an
  evidence-gated bundle evaluator, hooks that enforce what survives, and a funnel
  that notices when the loop has quietly stopped working. Standard library only,
  distributed as one deterministic zipapp.
keywords:
  - claude-code
  - self-improving-agents
  - recursive-self-improvement
  - agent-memory
  - agent-skills
  - ai-safety
